# openipc/br-ext-chip-hisilicon/board/hi3516cv6xx/hi3516cv6xx.generic.config
# (the shared config for every hi3516cv6xx board, not just this one) ships
# with "# CONFIG_TUN is not set". This device is the only one that needs
# it -- ar8030-tun (BR2_PACKAGE_AR8030_TUNTAP, see package/ar8030/Config.in)
# bridges a TUN device to the AR8030 RF link -- so it's layered on here via
# BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES instead of touching the shared
# board file every other hi3516cv6xx device also builds against.
#
# =m, not =y: matches ar8030-tun's own interfaces.d script, which does
# `modprobe tun` before starting it.
CONFIG_TUN=m
